.Dd June 1, 2025
.Dt XO_IS_EMITTING 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm xo_is_emitting , xo_is_emitting_h
.Nd test whether libxo will emit output at the current position
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libxo
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In libxo/xo.h
.Ft int
.Fn xo_is_emitting "void"
.Ft int
.Fn xo_is_emitting_h "xo_handle_t *xop"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
When a filter is in place, some output positions may be permanently
filtered out: the active filter has determined that no content
generated at the current position can ever appear in the final output.
.Pp
The
.Fn xo_is_emitting
function returns true when output at the current position of the default
handle will reach the final output.
Callers can use this to skip expensive computation that would otherwise
precede a call to
.Xr xo_emit 3 .
.Pp
The
.Fn xo_is_emitting_h
variant operates on the specified handle.
To use the default handle, pass a
.Dv NULL
handle.
.Pp
Both functions return true when:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
filtering is disabled,
.It
the filter module is not loaded, or
.It
the filter status is anything other than
.Dv XO_STATUS_DEAD
(for example
.Dv XO_STATUS_TRACK
or
.Dv XO_STATUS_PRED ,
which still require key and predicate fields to be evaluated before
a decision can be made).
.El
.Pp
Both functions return false only when the filter status is
.Dv XO_STATUS_DEAD :
the active filter has permanently discarded this output position.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns true
.Pq non-zero
when output at the current position will reach the final output.
Returns false
.Pq zero
when the current position is permanently filtered out
.Pq Dv XO_STATUS_DEAD .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
xo_open_container("interface-information");
if (xo_is_emitting()) {
    /* skip expensive work only when output will actually be seen */
    xo_open_container("connections");
    xo_emit("{:field/...}", value);
    xo_close_container("connections");
}
xo_close_container("interface-information");
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libxo 3 ,
.Xr xo_add_filter 3 ,
.Xr xo_emit 3 ,
.Xr xo_filter 7
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn xo_is_emitting
function first appeared in
.Fx 15.0 .
